      "text": "We are given the system of equations:\n\\[ x + y = 4 \\]\n\\[ 3xy = 4 \\]\n\nFirst, we solve the second equation for \\( xy \\):\n\\[ 3xy = 4 \\]\n\\[ xy = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( y = 4 - x \\) into the first equation:\n\\[ x + y = 4 \\]\n\\[ x + (4 - x) = 4 \\]\nThis equation is always true, so it doesn't give us new information. Instead, we use the product of the roots:\n\\[ xy = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\nWe substitute \\( y = 4 - x \\) into \\( xy = \\frac{4}{3} \\):\n\\[ x(4 - x) = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\\[ 4x - x^2 = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\\[ 3(4x - x^2) = 4 \\]\n\\[ 12x - 3x^2 = 4 \\]\n\\[ 3x^2 - 12x + 4 = 0 \\]\n\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 3 \\), \\( b = -12 \\), and \\( c = 4 \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{-(-12) \\pm \\sqrt{(-12)^2 - 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4}}{2 \\cdot 3} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{144 - 48}}{6} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{12 \\pm \\sqrt{96}}{6} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{12 \\pm 4\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\nThus, the solutions for \\( x \\) are:\n\\[ x = \\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{6 - 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\nWe can express these solutions in the form \\( x = \\frac{a \\pm b\\sqrt{c}}{d} \\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} = \\frac{6}{3} \\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} = 2 \\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{6 - 2\\sqrt{6}}{3} = \\frac{6}{3} \\mp \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} = 2 \\mp \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\nSo, the solutions are:\n\\[ x = 2 + \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}, \\quad x = 2 - \\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\]\n\nHere, \\( a = 6 \\), \\( b = 2 \\), \\( c = 6 \\), and \\( d = 3 \\). Therefore, \\( a + b + c + d = 6 + 2 + 6 + 3 = 17 \\).\n\nThe value of \\( a + b + c + d \\) is \\(\\boxed{17}\\).",
